 **Parallelism and Data Flow:**
 *   The four pipelines (Pipeline 0–3) operate in parallel, processing adjacent voxel or sample values in the x-direction [S2, unofficial].
-*   Each pipeline is connected to its immediate neighbor by shift registers in each major unit (Interpolation, Gradient, Shading, Classification, Compositing) [S2, unofficial]. These shift registers provide values to neighbors in the same cycle [S2, unofficial].
-*   The pipelines on the far left (Pipeline 0) and far right (Pipeline 3) are connected in a wrap-around fashion [S1]. Specifically, the shift registers of the rightmost pipeline recirculate values needed in the next cycle and send them to the leftmost pipeline [S1][S2, unofficial].
